# Line endings.
#
# Source files are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out with the
# platform's convention, as usual. Two exceptions matter here:
#
#  * Real binaries (PDF, images, spreadsheets, fonts) must never have their
#    bytes rewritten. Git's own auto-detection is not enough on Windows, where
#    a clone with core.autocrlf=true inserted carriage returns into the
#    generated PDF fixtures — which both corrupts them and makes a freshly
#    cloned tree look dirty the moment `python scripts/gen_fixtures.py` runs.
#
#  * Everything under tests/fixtures/ is byte-exact by design. The generator
#    writes those files, and the checked-in copies must be what it writes, so
#    that regenerating on a fresh clone leaves `git status` clean. That
#    includes the CSVs, whose CRLF row endings are the format, not a platform
#    artefact.
* text=auto

*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

tests/fixtures/** -text
